==English==
{{was wotd|2019|August|7}}

===Etymology===
{{multiple images
|direction = vertical
|image1 = Crescentia cujete WS.JPG
|caption1 = The calabash or [[calabash tree]] ({{taxlink|Crescentia cujete|species|ver=190425}}; ''sense 1'')
}}

From {{der|en|fr|calebasse}}, from {{der|en|es|calabaça}}, {{m|es|calabaza||gourd; pumpkin}}, possibly from {{der|en|ar|قَرْعَة يَابِسَة|tr=qarʿa yābisa||dry gourd}} or directly from its {{glossary|etymon}} {{der|en|fa|خربزه|tr=xarboza, xarboze||melon}},<ref name="OED">{{R:OED Online|pos=n|id=26129|date=1888}}</ref><ref>{{R:Oxford Dictionaries Online}}</ref> possibly ultimately from {{der|en|sa|त्रपुस||colocynth fruit}} (compare {{noncog|fa|تربز|tr=tarboz(e)||watermelon}}). The English word is cognate with {{cog|ca|carabassa||pumpkin; orange colour}}, {{cog|gl|cabaza||gourd, pumpkin, squash; calabash (container)}}, {{cog|oc|calebasso}}, {{m|oc|carabasso}}, {{m|oc|carbasso}}, {{cog|pt|cabaça||gourd; calabash (container)}}, {{cog|scn|caravazza}}.<ref name="OED"/>

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|en|/ˈkæləbæʃ/}}
* {{a|GA}} {{IPA|en|/ˈkæləˌbæʃ/}}
* {{hyphenation|en|ca|la|bash}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|es}}

# A [[tree]] (known as the [[calabash tree]]; {{taxlink|Crescentia cujete|species|ver=190425}}) [[native#Adjective|native]] to [[Central America|Central]] and [[South America]], the [[West Indies]], and southern [[Florida]], [[bear#Verb|bearing]] [[large]], [[round#Adjective|round]] [[fruit#Noun|fruit]] used to make [[container]]s ''(sense 3)''; the fruit of this tree.
# The [[bottle gourd]] ([[calabash vine]], ''[[Lagenaria siceraria]]''), believed to have [[originate]]d in [[Africa]] which is grown for its fruit that are used as a [[vegetable]] and to make containers ''(sense 3)''; the fruit of this plant.
# A container made from the [[mature#Adjective|mature]], [[dried#Adjective|dried]] [[shell#Noun|shell]] of the fruit of one of the above plants; also, a similarly [[shaped#Adjective|shaped]] container made from some other [[material#Noun|material]].
#* {{quote-book|lang=en| year=1851| author={{w|Herman Melville}}| title={{w|Moby Dick}}| section=Chapter 13| passage=The people of his island of Rokovoko, it seems, at their wedding feasts express the fragrant water of young cocoanuts into a large stained '''calabash''' like a punchbowl; and this punchbowl always forms the great central ornament on the braided mat where the feast is held.}}
# A calabash and its [[contents]]; as much as [[fill#Verb|fills]] such a container.
# {{lb|en|musical instrument}} A [[musical instrument]], most commonly a [[drum#Noun|drum]] or [[rattle#Noun|rattle]], made from a calabash fruit.

